{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a7f1e57ec45cbbe6","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tstatus: completed\n3\tspec: [004-bug-job-failure-reason]\n4\tsummary: 'Split BackoffLimitExceeded from DeadlineExceeded in the job failure classifier: added pod_oom_killed reason, pod-resolution reason composition (reason + exit code in published text), internal regression tests, and CHANGELOG entry'\n5\texecution_id: agent-task-executor-failreason-exec-005-spec-004-bug-job-failure-reason\n6\tdark-factory-version: dev\n7\tcreated: \"2026-08-31T23:55:00Z\"\n8\tqueued: \"2026-08-31T22:03:30Z\"\n9\tstarted: \"2026-08-31T22:03:31Z\"\n10\tcompleted: \"2026-08-31T22:11:18Z\"\n11\tbranch: dark-factory/bug-job-failure-reason\n12\t---\n13\t\n14\t<summary>\n15\t- A Job that exhausted its retry backoff limit is no longer mislabeled `deadline_exceeded`; only a genuine active-deadline kill still reports `deadline_exceeded`.\n16\t- A new machine-readable reason value `pod_oom_killed` is added to the closed reason set for OOM-killed pods, so operators can grep for OOM kills specifically.\n17\t- For backoff-limit failures, the published failure text now carries the pod's actual termination reason and exit code (e.g. `OOMKilled`/`137`) — no manual `kubectl get pod -o json` needed.\n18\t- Non-OOM pod deaths under a backoff-limit failure surface their own termination reason + exit code (e.g. `Error`/`1`) under the existing generic pod-failure reason, never `deadline_exceeded` and never `pod_oom_killed`.\n19\t- When the failed pod is no longer resolvable (GC'd or lister not synced), the Job still publishes a distinct non-deadline reason, just without pod detail.\n20\t- The executor log line and the vault task's `## Failure` body show the same specific reason string.\n21\t- The two existing tests that pinned the wrong `deadline_exceeded` mapping are corrected; new regression tests lock the OOM path and the non-OOM path.\n22\t- A `## Unreleased` CHANGELOG section is created for this fix.\n23\t</summary>\n24\t\n25\t<objective>\n26\tFix the job-failure classifier so a Job that hit `BackoffLimitExceeded` publishes a distinct pod-failure reason that surfaces the pod's terminated reason + exit code (with a dedicated `pod_oom_killed` for OOM kills), never the misleading `deadline_exceeded`, while leaving the genuine deadline path unchanged. Motivating incident (2026-08-16): a pod OOM-killed at ~6 min of a 30-min budget was reported as `deadline_exceeded`, and three genuinely different failures were all logged identically, misdirecting a post-mortem that tallied 82 Jobs as quota-starved.\n27\t</objective>\n28\t\n29\t<context>\n30\tRead `/home/node/.claude/CLAUDE.md` for project conventions (Ginkgo/Gomega v2, `github.com/bborbe/errors` wrapping, counterfeiter mocks, glog V(n) gating, coverage ≥80% for new code).\n31\t\n32\tRead these files fully before changing anything:\n33\t- `/workspace/pkg/job_watcher.go` — `JobFailureReason` (lines ~249-267), `HandleJob` (lines ~139-162), `handleTerminal` (lines ~164-182), `publishSyntheticFailure` (lines ~184-197), `PodLister()` (lines ~131-137), the `podLister atomic.Pointer[corev1listers.PodLister]` field (line 65), and the existing `classifyPodFailure`/`ownerJobName` helpers (lines ~320-363). Note `ownerJobName(pod)` already returns the owning Job name from a Pod's ownerRefs — reuse it.\n34\t- `/workspace/pkg/zombie_reason.go` — the closed `ZombieReason` set and its doc contract (\"Adding a new value requires updating this list and the documentation\").\n35\t- `/workspace/pkg/job_watcher_test.go` — the two `BackoffLimitExceeded` assertions to correct (HandleJob path ~line 240, direct-mapping path ~line 271) and the two `DeadlineExceeded` assertions that must stay (lines ~220 and ~262).\n36\t- `/workspace/pkg/zombie_reason_test.go` — the per-value `String()` assertions to extend.\n37\t- `/workspace/pkg/zombie_sweeper_test.go` — the informer-indexer pattern for building a test `PodLister` without starting informers (search `podInformer.GetIndexer().Add` / `informerFactory.Core().V1().Pods().Lister()`); mirror it in the new internal test file below.\n38\t- `/workspace/pkg/result_publisher.go` — `PublishFailure` (lines ~171-230) writes the reason verbatim into the vault `## Failure` body's `- **Reason:**` line; this is why the composed reason string must keep the greppable value as its leading token.\n39\t\n40\tRelevant docs (in-container paths):\n41\t- `/home/node/.claude/plugins/marketplaces/coding/docs/go-testing-guide.md` — Ginkgo/Gomega, external test packages, coverage ≥80%.\n42\t- `/home/node/.claude/plugins/marketplaces/coding/docs/go-error-wrapping-guide.md` — never `fmt.Errorf`; `fmt.Sprintf` for string building is an established pattern (see `result_publisher.go`).\n43\t- `/home/node/.claude/plugins/marketplaces/coding/docs/go-glog-guide.md` — `glog.V(2)` for per-failure events, `glog.Errorf` for lister lookup errors.\n44\t- `/home/node/.claude/plugins/marketplaces/coding/docs/changelog-guide.md` — `## Unreleased` format and prefix rules.\n45\t- `/home/node/.claude/plugins/marketplaces/coding/docs/definition-of-done.md` — coverage rules for new code.\n46\t</context>\n47\t\n48\t<requirements>\n49\t1. Add the new reason value in `/workspace/pkg/zombie_reason.go`. Add `ZombieReasonPodOOMKilled` to the const block after `ZombieReasonTypeMismatch`, keeping the existing alignment style (gofmt normalizes):\n50\t   ```go\n51\t   ZombieReasonPodOOMKilled      ZombieReason = \"pod_oom_killed\"\n52\t   ```\n53\t   Update the package doc comment (the `ZombieReason` block comment) so it states the new contract: OOM kills use the dedicated `pod_oom_killed` value so operators can grep for OOM specifically; other non-zero pod terminations fall back to the generic `pod_crash_no_stdout`. Keep the existing \"adding a value requires updating this list and the documentation\" sentence.\n54\t\n55\t2. Add the matching `String()` assertion in `/workspace/pkg/zombie_reason_test.go`, inside the `Describe(\"String()\", ...)` block (after the `type_mismatch` `It`):\n56\t   ```go\n57\t   It(\"returns pod_oom_killed for ZombieReasonPodOOMKilled\", func() {\n58\t       Expect(pkg.ZombieReasonPodOOMKilled.String()).To(Equal(\"pod_oom_killed\"))\n59\t   })\n60\t   ```\n61\t\n62\t3. Split the classifier in `/workspace/pkg/job_watcher.go`. Replace the body of `JobFailureReason` so `BackoffLimitExceeded` maps to the generic pod-failure reason instead of `ZombieReasonDeadlineExceeded`, and update its doc comment. Do NOT merge the two conditions — a `DeadlineExceeded` condition always yields `deadline_exceeded`, even if a `BackoffLimitExceeded` condition is also present. New form:\n63\t   ```go\n64\t   // JobFailureReason maps a failed Job's conditions to a ZombieReason. Returns\n65\t   // ZombieReasonDeadlineExceeded when a Failed condition has Reason\n66\t   // \"DeadlineExceeded\" (the kubelet killed the pod for running past\n67\t   // activeDeadlineSeconds). Returns the generic pod-failure reason\n68\t   // ZombieReasonPodCrashNoStdout for \"BackoffLimitExceeded\" (the Job exhausted\n69\t   // its retry backoff limit — a distinct reason from a deadline kill; HandleJob\n70\t   // resolves the pod's terminated reason + exit code and surfaces them in the\n71\t   // published reason) and for any other Failed condition (the pod terminated\n72\t   // non-zero and no AgentResult was observed; the Job-condition informer only\n73\t   // fires AFTER terminal state, so absence of an AgentResult is implicit at this\n74\t   // point).\n75\t   func JobFailureReason(job *batchv1.Job) ZombieReason {\n76\t       for _, c := range job.Status.Conditions {\n77\t           if c.Type == batchv1.JobFailed && c.Status == corev1.ConditionTrue {\n78\t               switch c.Reason {\n79\t               case \"DeadlineExceeded\":\n80\t                   return ZombieReasonDeadlineExceeded\n81\t               case \"BackoffLimitExceeded\":\n82\t                   return ZombieReasonPodCrashNoStdout\n83\t               }\n84\t           }\n85\t       }\n86\t       return ZombieReasonPodCrashNoStdout\n87\t   }\n88\t   ```\n89\t\n90\t4. Add a package-level condition helper near `IsJobFailed`:\n91\t   ```go\n92\t   // isBackoffLimitExceeded reports whether the Job's terminal Failed condition\n93\t   // has Reason \"BackoffLimitExceeded\" (the Job exhausted its retry backoff\n94\t   // limit).\n95\t   func isBackoffLimitExceeded(job *batchv1.Job) bool {\n96\t       for _, c := range job.Status.Conditions {\n97\t           if c.Type == batchv1.JobFailed && c.Status == corev1.ConditionTrue && c.Reason == \"BackoffLimitExceeded\" {\n98\t               return true\n99\t           }\n100\t       }\n101\t       return false\n102\t   }\n103\t   ```\n104\t\n105\t5. Add a package-level pod-state helper:\n106\t   ```go\n107\t   // hasNonZeroTerminatedContainer reports whether any container terminated with\n108\t   // a non-zero exit code.\n109\t   func hasNonZeroTerminatedContainer(pod *corev1.Pod) bool {\n110\t       for _, cs := range pod.Status.ContainerStatuses {\n111\t           if cs.State.Terminated != nil && cs.State.Terminated.ExitCode != 0 {\n112\t               return true\n113\t           }\n114\t       }\n115\t       return false\n116\t   }\n117\t   ```\n118\t\n119\t6. Add the pod-resolution method on `*jobWatcher`. It resolves the Job's most recently created pod from the shared pod lister (matched by Job owner reference via the existing `ownerJobName` helper) and returns its `.state.terminated.reason` and `exitCode`. Every failure path returns `ok=false` with no side effects — never a panic:\n120\t   ```go\n121\t   // terminalPodDetail returns the terminated reason and exit code of the Job's\n122\t   // most recently created pod that has a non-zero terminated container, matched\n123\t   // by Job owner reference. ok is false when the pod lister is not yet synced,\n124\t   // the lister lookup fails, or no owned pod carries a non-zero terminated\n125\t   // container.\n126\t   func (w *jobWatcher) terminalPodDetail(job *batchv1.Job) (terminatedReason string, exitCode int32, ok bool) {\n127\t       lister := w.PodLister()\n128\t       if lister == nil {\n129\t           return \"\", 0, false\n130\t       }\n131\t       pods, err := lister.Pods(job.Namespace).List(labels.Everything())\n132\t       if err != nil {\n133\t           glog.Errorf(\"job watcher: list pods for job %s/%s: %v\", job.Namespace, job.Name, err)\n134\t           return \"\", 0, false\n135\t       }\n136\t       var best *corev1.Pod\n137\t       for _, pod := range pods {\n138\t           if ownerJobName(pod) != job.Name {\n139\t               continue\n140\t           }\n141\t           if !hasNonZeroTerminatedContainer(pod) {\n142\t               continue\n143\t           }\n144\t           if best == nil || pod.CreationTimestamp.After(best.CreationTimestamp.Time) {\n145\t               best = pod\n146\t           }\n147\t       }\n148\t       if best == nil {\n149\t           return \"\", 0, false\n150\t       }\n151\t       for _, cs := range best.Status.ContainerStatuses {\n152\t           if cs.State.Terminated != nil && cs.State.Terminated.ExitCode != 0 {\n153\t               return cs.State.Terminated.Reason, cs.State.Terminated.ExitCode, true\n154\t           }\n155\t       }\n156\t       return \"\", 0, false\n157\t   }\n158\t   ```\n159\t\n160\t7. Add the reason-composition methods on `*jobWatcher`. The published reason string keeps the machine-readable `ZombieReason` value as its leading token and appends the pod detail in parentheses; the spec leaves the exact detail format to you and this is the chosen format. Use `fmt.Sprintf` (established in `result_publisher.go`), never `fmt.Errorf`:\n161\t   ```go\n162\t   // failureReason returns the reason string to publish for a failed Job. A\n163\t   // BackoffLimitExceeded failure surfaces the pod's terminated reason + exit\n164\t   // code when the pod is still resolvable (see backoffFailureReason); every\n165\t   // other failure publishes the bare ZombieReason value.\n166\t   func (w *jobWatcher) failureReason(job *batchv1.Job) string {\n167\t       reason := JobFailureReason(job)\n168\t       if reason == ZombieReasonDeadlineExceeded || !isBackoffLimitExceeded(job) {\n169\t           return reason.String()\n170\t       }\n171\t       return w.backoffFailureReason(job, reason)\n172\t   }\n173\t\n174\t   // backoffFailureReason classifies a BackoffLimitExceeded Job using its\n175\t   // resolved pod's terminal state: the dedicated pod_oom_killed for an OOMKilled\n176\t   // pod, else the generic pod-failure reason, always appending the terminated\n177\t   // reason + exit code when a pod is resolvable so operators see the cause\n178\t   // without inspecting the pod.\n179\t   func (w *jobWatcher) backoffFailureReason(job *batchv1.Job, base ZombieReason) string {\n180\t       terminatedReason, exitCode, ok := w.terminalPodDetail(job)\n181\t       if !ok {\n182\t           return base.String()\n183\t       }\n184\t       if terminatedReason == \"OOMKilled\" {\n185\t           return fmt.Sprintf(\"%s (%s/%d)\", ZombieReasonPodOOMKilled, terminatedReason, exitCode)\n186\t       }\n187\t       return fmt.Sprintf(\"%s (%s/%d)\", base.String(), terminatedReason, exitCode)\n188\t   }\n189\t   ```\n190\t   Add `\"fmt\"` to the stdlib import group and `\"k8s.io/apimachinery/pkg/labels\"` to the k8s import group in this file. Do not worry about final import ordering — the precommit `format` step (goimports-reviser) normalizes it.\n191\t\n192\t8. Wire the composition into `HandleJob` and the publish path (no interface change to `ResultPublisher`):\n193\t   - In `HandleJob`, change `reason := JobFailureReason(job)` to `reason := w.failureReason(job)`. The variable becomes a `string`; the existing `glog.V(2).Infof(\"job %s/%s failed (task %s): %s\", job.Namespace, job.Name, taskID, reason)` and `w.handleTerminal(ctx, taskID, job, reason, true)` calls keep working unchanged. This makes the executor log line show the same specific reason as the published failure.\n194\t   - Change `handleTerminal`'s `reason ZombieReason` parameter to `reason string` (no other behavior change).\n195\t   - Change `publishSyntheticFailure`'s `reason ZombieReason` parameter to `reason string`, and change the `PublishFailure` call from `reason.String()` to `reason` — the reason string flows through `PublishFailure`'s existing `(ctx, task, jobName, reason string)` signature as-is.\n196\t   - Do NOT change `ResultPublisher` or the `PublishFailure` signature.\n197\t   - Spec Failure Mode row 5 (executor crashes mid-publish after classifying) is pre-existing behavior, NOT new work: `PublishFailure` is at-least-once via Kafka and its dedupe (keyed on job name) in `/workspace/pkg/result_publisher.go` already absorbs re-delivery. Do not modify that dedupe code.\n198\t\n199\t9. Correct the two wrong `BackoffLimitExceeded` tests in `/workspace/pkg/job_watcher_test.go`:\n200\t   - HandleJob path (~line 240): rename the spec to \"maps BackoffLimitExceeded job condition to pod_crash_no_stdout (no resolvable pod)\" and change the final assertion from `Expect(calledReason).To(Equal(\"deadline_exceeded\"))` to `Expect(calledReason).To(Equal(\"pod_crash_no_stdout\"))`. This test runs against a watcher whose pod lister was never populated (`Run()` is never called, so `PodLister()` returns nil) — it exercises the nil-lister path of `terminalPodDetail` and proves the reason is distinct from `deadline_exceeded`.\n201\t   - Direct-mapping path (~line 271): rename to \"returns pod_crash_no_stdout for BackoffLimitExceeded\" and change the assertion from `pkg.ZombieReasonDeadlineExceeded` to `pkg.ZombieReasonPodCrashNoStdout`.\n202\t   - Do NOT touch the two `DeadlineExceeded` assertions (lines ~220 and ~262) — they must keep asserting `deadline_exceeded`.\n203\t\n204\t10. Add an internal test file `/workspace/pkg/job_watcher_internal_test.go` in `package pkg` (this pairs an internal test file with the existing external one, matching the repo's `main_test.go` + `main_internal_test.go` precedent). It exists because the OOM/backoff pod-resolution path needs a populated pod lister on the real watcher, and `Run()` is never called in tests so `PodLister()` would otherwise return nil.\n205\t    - Helper `newTestPodLister(pods ...*corev1.Pod) corev1listers.PodLister`: create `fake.NewSimpleClientset()`, then `k8sinformers.NewSharedInformerFactoryWithOptions(fakeClient, 0, k8sinformers.WithNamespace(\"test-ns\"))`, add each pod with `_ = informerFactory.Core().V1().Pods().Informer().GetIndexer().Add(pod)`, and return `informerFactory.Core().V1().Pods().Lister()` — mirror the exact pattern in `/workspace/pkg/zombie_sweeper_test.go`.\n206\t    - Helper `setPodLister(w JobWatcher, pods ...*corev1.Pod)`: `lister := newTestPodLister(pods...)` then `w.(*jobWatcher).podLister.Store(&lister)`.\n207\t    - `BeforeEach`: `ctx = context.Background()`, `fakePublisher = &mocks.FakeResultPublisher{}`, `taskStore = NewTaskStore()`, `watcher = NewJobWatcher(fake.NewSimpleClientset(), \"test-ns\", taskStore, fakePublisher)`, and a `testTask`/`testTaskID` pair mirroring the external file's setup (task type `lib.Task` from `github.com/bborbe/agent`, frontmatter with `status`/`assignee`).\n208\t    - Helper `makeJob(name, taskID string, conditions ...batchv1.JobCondition) *batchv1.Job`: same shape as the external file (namespace `\"test-ns\"`, label `agent.benjamin-borbe.de/task-id`, `Status.Conditions` from args).\n209\t    - Helper `backoffCondition() batchv1.JobCondition`: `{Type: batchv1.JobFailed, Status: corev1.ConditionTrue, Reason: \"BackoffLimitExceeded\", Message: \"Job has reached the specified backoff limit\"}`.\n210\t    - Helper `makeOwnedTerminatedPod(name, jobName, taskID, terminatedReason string, exitCode int32, createdAt string) *corev1.Pod`: namespace `\"test-ns\"`, labels `{\"agent.benjamin-borbe.de/task-id\": taskID}`, `OwnerReferences: []metav1.OwnerReference{{Kind: \"Job\", Name: jobName}}`, `Status.Phase = corev1.PodFailed`, `Status.ContainerStatuses = []corev1.ContainerStatus{{State: corev1.ContainerState{Terminated: &corev1.ContainerStateTerminated{Reason: terminatedReason, ExitCode: exitCode}}}}`, and `CreationTimestamp = metav1.NewTime(t)` parsed from `createdAt` (RFC3339) when non-empty.\n211\t    - Then add these Ginkgo specs (each: `taskStore.Store(testTaskID, testTask)`, `watcher.HandleJob(ctx, job)`, assert `fakePublisher.PublishFailureCallCount()` is 1, capture `_, _, _, calledReason := fakePublisher.PublishFailureArgsForCall(0)`):\n212\t      a. OOMKilled pod resolvable → `Expect(calledReason).To(Equal(\"pod_oom_killed (OOMKilled/137)\"))` and `Expect(calledReason).NotTo(ContainSubstring(\"deadline_exceeded\"))`. This one spec satisfies ACs 2a, 3, and 4.\n213\t      b. Non-OOM terminated pod (`Error`/exit `1`) → `Expect(calledReason).To(Equal(\"pod_crash_no_stdout (Error/1)\"))`, plus `NotTo(ContainSubstring(\"deadline_exceeded\"))` and `NotTo(ContainSubstring(\"pod_oom_killed\"))`. Satisfies AC 2b.\n214\t      c. Two pods owned by the same job with different terminated reasons (earlier `Error`/`1`, later `OOMKilled`/`137` — distinct `createdAt` timestamps) → `Expect(calledReason).To(Equal(\"pod_oom_killed (OOMKilled/137)\"))`, proving the terminal (last) pod's state is used (spec Failure Mode row 4).\n215\t      d. Empty lister cache (no pods) → `Expect(calledReason).To(Equal(\"pod_crash_no_stdout\"))` with no detail (spec Failure Mode rows 1 and 3).\n216\t      e. An owned pod with no non-zero terminated container (e.g. `corev1.PodRunning` with no terminated state) → `Expect(calledReason).To(Equal(\"pod_crash_no_stdout\"))` with no detail.\n217\t\n218\t11. Add the CHANGELOG entry in `/workspace/CHANGELOG.md`: create `## Unreleased` directly under the `# Changelog` heading (none exists at HEAD v0.8.0) with one bullet following the changelog-guide format:\n219\t    ```\n220\t    ## Unreleased\n221\t\n222\t    - fix: split `BackoffLimitExceeded` from `DeadlineExceeded` in the job failure classifier — a Job that exhausted its backoff limit now publishes the pod's terminated reason + exit code (dedicated `pod_oom_killed` for OOM kills) instead of a misleading `deadline_exceeded`\n223\t    ```\n224\t\n225\t12. Do NOT touch `pkg/zombie_sweeper.go`'s `classify` deadline fallback — the spec's Non-goal explicitly defers it as a follow-up.\n226\t</requirements>\n227\t\n228\t<constraints>\n229\t- Repo conventions are frozen: Ginkgo/Gomega v2 tests (no stdlib table tests), `github.com/bborbe/errors` wrapping (never `fmt.Errorf`), counterfeiter mocks for any new dependency, glog `V(n)` gating.\n230\t- `ZombieReason` is a closed machine-readable set (`pkg/zombie_reason.go`). The new `pod_oom_killed` value is added deliberately and documented in the doc comment, which states that adding a value requires updating the list and the documentation.\n231\t- Do NOT change `PublishFailure`'s interface or signature — the reason string flows through as-is. You may change the internal `handleTerminal`/`publishSyntheticFailure` parameter type from `ZombieReason` to `string`.\n232\t- Assumption: the failed Job's pod is usually still resolvable at `HandleJob` time (`TTLSecondsAfterFinished` keeps it until TTL expiry). When it is not (pod GC'd / lister not synced / lister nil), the Job-condition path still publishes a distinct pod-failure reason without pod detail — never `deadline_exceeded`.\n233\t- The two existing `DeadlineExceeded` assertions in `pkg/job_watcher_test.go` stay; the two `BackoffLimitExceeded` assertions that pin the wrong behavior are updated.\n234\t- CHANGELOG: add an `## Unreleased` bullet for this fix (creating the section if absent — none exists at HEAD v0.8.0).\n235\t- Non-goals are load-bearing: do NOT raise the Job memory limit, do NOT fix the GitHub App `workflows`-scope permission, do NOT touch the resync `not in task store` warning noise, do NOT touch `zombie_sweeper.go`'s `classify` deadline fallback.\n236\t- Do NOT commit — dark-factory handles git.\n237\t- Existing tests must still pass.\n238\t</constraints>\n239\t\n240\t<verification>\n241\tRun `make test` iteratively after each meaningful change (fast feedback loop), then `make precommit` ONCE at the very end.\n242\t\n243\t- `make test` — exits 0.\n244\t- `make precommit` — exits 0.\n245\t- `go test -mod=mod -coverprofile=/tmp/cover.out ./pkg/... && go tool cover -func=/tmp/cover.out` — confirm the new functions (`failureReason`, `backoffFailureReason`, `terminalPodDetail`, `isBackoffLimitExceeded`, `hasNonZeroTerminatedContainer`) are each exercised by at least one test (≥80% statement coverage for new code).\n246\t- `grep -n 'BackoffLimitExceeded' pkg/job_watcher.go` — returns at least one line that does NOT map to `ZombieReasonDeadlineExceeded` (acceptance-criterion evidence).\n247\t- `grep -n 'pod_oom_killed' pkg/zombie_reason.go pkg/zombie_reason_test.go pkg/job_watcher.go pkg/job_watcher_internal_test.go` — shows the new value in the closed set, its `String()` assertion, and its production usage.\n248\t\n249\tDo NOT run `docker`, `make build`, `kubectl`, or `dark-factory` commands in this prompt — those are operator-executable and belong on the spec's verification ladder.\n250\t</verification>\n251\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b68d74ad5231f9ea","session_id":"3667b84f-c892-4ca5-8115-a830204bf3b3","uuid":"24a70199-981b-479a-8982-b61c86d76178","timestamp":"2026-09-03T17:58:40.431Z","subagent_type":"dark-factory:prompt-creator","task_description":"Generate prompts from spec 005"}
