{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b00ee739fc259094","type":"tool_result","content":"/home/node/go/pkg/mod/github.com/bborbe/agent@v0.85.1/CHANGELOG.md:609:- chore(task/controller): drop `agent-task-controller-netpol.yaml` — the K3s+Flannel cluster does not enforce NetworkPolicies; gateway-secret auth on git-rest is the operative defense. Goal [[Enable NetworkPolicy enforcement on K3s cluster]] tracks reintroducing real enforcement.\n/home/node/go/pkg/mod/github.com/bborbe/agent@v0.85.1/CHANGELOG.md:613:- feat(task/controller): gitrestclient sends `X-Gateway-Secret` + `X-Gateway-Initator` headers on `/api/v1/*` calls when `GATEWAY_SECRET` is set; matches git-rest spec 004 auth contract\n/home/node/go/pkg/mod/github.com/bborbe/agent@v0.85.1/CHANGELOG.md:614:- feat(task/controller): add `GATEWAY_SECRET` env / `--gateway-secret` flag (sourced from `OBSIDIAN_OPENCLAW_GATEWAY_SECRET` teamvault key in dev/prod manifests)\n/home/node/go/pkg/mod/github.com/bborbe/agent@v0.85.1/helm/README.md:177:| `controller.gatewaySecret` | `\"\"` | Gateway secret value (chart-created Secret key `gateway-secret`). |\n/home/node/go/pkg/mod/github.com/bborbe/agent@v0.85.1/helm/values.yaml:248:  #   # Gateway secret value (key gateway-secret). Same Secret as sentry-dsn.\n/home/node/go/pkg/mod/github.com/bborbe/agent@v0.85.1/helm/values.yaml:250:  #   # Name of a pre-existing Secret providing keys sentry-dsn + gateway-secret.\n/home/node/go/pkg/mod/github.com/bborbe/agent@v0.85.1/helm/templates/controller-secret.yaml:18:  gateway-secret: {{ $c.gatewaySecret | b64enc | quote }}\n/home/node/go/pkg/mod/github.com/bborbe/agent@v0.85.1/helm/templates/controller-statefulset.yaml:69:            - name: GATEWAY_SECRET\n/home/node/go/pkg/mod/github.com/bborbe/agent@v0.85.1/helm/templates/controller-statefulset.yaml:73:                  key: gateway-secret\n/home/node/go/pkg/mod/github.com/bborbe/agent@v0.85.1/prompts/completed/096-gitrestclient-gateway-secret-auth.md:3:summary: 'Wired shared-secret auth into task/controller gitrestclient: added gatewaySecret/gatewayInitiator fields, setAuthHeaders helper (called in Get/Post/Delete/List, not IsReady), updated NewGitRestClient and NewGitRestClientForTest signatures, added 8 new test cases (q-x), added GatewaySecret field to main.go, added gateway-secret to K8s Secret manifest sourced via teamvaultPassword, added GATEWAY_SECRET secretKeyRef to StatefulSet, and updated CHANGELOG.'\n/home/node/go/pkg/mod/github.com/bborbe/agent@v0.85.1/prompts/completed/096-gitrestclient-gateway-secret-auth.md:4:container: agent-096-gitrestclient-gateway-secret-auth\n/home/node/go/pkg/mod/github.com/bborbe/agent@v0.85.1/prompts/completed/096-gitrestclient-gateway-secret-auth.md:15:- Two new headers go on every file-API call: `X-Gateway-Secret` (the shared secret) and `X-Gateway-Initator` (caller identity, deliberate misspelling per the contract).\n/home/node/go/pkg/mod/github.com/bborbe/agent@v0.85.1/prompts/completed/096-gitrestclient-gateway-secret-auth.md:17:- The controller reads the secret from a new `GATEWAY_SECRET` env var; the K8s manifest sources it from a teamvault-backed Secret data key.\n/home/node/go/pkg/mod/github.com/bborbe/agent@v0.85.1/prompts/completed/096-gitrestclient-gateway-secret-auth.md:22:Wire shared-secret auth into the controller's git-rest HTTP client so it can talk to the auth-enabled `vault-obsidian-openclaw` service. After this prompt, every `/api/v1/*` call from the controller carries `X-Gateway-Secret` and `X-Gateway-Initator: agent-task-controller`; the IsReady probe stays header-free.\n/home/node/go/pkg/mod/github.com/bborbe/agent@v0.85.1/prompts/completed/096-gitrestclient-gateway-secret-auth.md:34:- `X-Gateway-Secret` — the configured shared secret value, exact string match.\n/home/node/go/pkg/mod/github.com/bborbe/agent@v0.85.1/prompts/completed/096-gitrestclient-gateway-secret-auth.md:41:- Missing / wrong `X-Gateway-Secret` → HTTP 401 with body `secret in header 'X-Gateway-Secret' is invalid => access denied`.\n/home/node/go/pkg/mod/github.com/bborbe/agent@v0.85.1/prompts/completed/096-gitrestclient-gateway-secret-auth.md:42:- The server strips `X-Gateway-Secret` before the inner handler, so headers are not echoed back.\n/home/node/go/pkg/mod/github.com/bborbe/agent@v0.85.1/prompts/completed/096-gitrestclient-gateway-secret-auth.md:45:- When the controller's `GATEWAY_SECRET` is empty / unset, it sends NO auth headers. This keeps tests against an in-process httptest server straightforward and lets the controller continue to talk to a git-rest that has auth disabled.\n/home/node/go/pkg/mod/github.com/bborbe/agent@v0.85.1/prompts/completed/096-gitrestclient-gateway-secret-auth.md:53:- `task/controller/k8s/agent-task-controller-secret.yaml` — currently has only `sentry-dsn` (data key sourced via `teamvaultUrl`). Add a `gateway-secret` data key sourced via `'{{ \"OBSIDIAN_OPENCLAW_GATEWAY_SECRET\" | env | teamvaultPassword | base64 }}'`. Use `teamvaultPassword` (NOT `teamvaultUrl`) — the value lives in teamvault's password field, matching how `vault-obsidian-openclaw-secret.yaml` (the git-rest server side) reads the same env var. Both ends MUST resolve to the same string for auth to work.\n/home/node/go/pkg/mod/github.com/bborbe/agent@v0.85.1/prompts/completed/096-gitrestclient-gateway-secret-auth.md:54:- `task/controller/k8s/agent-task-controller-sts.yaml` — env list. Add `GATEWAY_SECRET` via `secretKeyRef` against the new data key.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b68d74ad5231f9ea","session_id":"3667b84f-c892-4ca5-8115-a830204bf3b3","uuid":"88b7e7b8-5e15-4560-ba95-ed38b772bfc1","timestamp":"2026-09-03T18:00:14.613Z","subagent_type":"dark-factory:prompt-creator","task_description":"Generate prompts from spec 005"}
