{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-891057aaf330eb88","type":"tool_result","content":"52\t1. Add the reconcile interval constant to `/workspace/pkg/handler/task_event_handler.go`, directly after the `concurrencyCapRetryDelay` const (line 54):\n53\t```go\n54\t// defaultReconcileIntervalSeconds is the interval between reconcile-loop passes\n55\t// (spec 005). Mirrors DefaultZombieSweeperIntervalSeconds: a package constant,\n56\t// not a CRD field and not env-configurable in this change. 60s is a reasonable\n57\t// recovery latency for a task whose deferral was lost across a restart.\n58\tconst defaultReconcileIntervalSeconds = 60 * time.Second\n59\t\n60\t// reconcilePassTimeout bounds one reconcile pass so a slow or large vault\n61\t// cannot hold a pass open indefinitely (spec 005 Failure Modes: \"Pass bounded\n62\t// by a per-pass timeout; logs evaluate count so cost is visible\"). Half the\n63\t// interval: a pass completes within a tick and leaves headroom for the next\n64\t// tick. Package constant — not configurable in this change.\n65\tconst reconcilePassTimeout = 30 * time.Second\n66\t```\n67\t\n68\t2. Create `/workspace/pkg/handler/task_file.go` (package `handler`) with the frontmatter/body extraction and task-file parsing helpers, ported from the controller's scanner (keep the BSD header):\n69\t```go\n70\t// Copyright (c) 2026 Benjamin Borbe All rights reserved.\n71\t// Use of this source code is governed by a BSD-style\n72\t// license that can be found in the LICENSE file.\n73\t\n74\tpackage handler\n75\t\n76\timport (\n77\t\t\"context\"\n78\t\t\"strings\"\n79\t\n80\t\tlib \"github.com/bborbe/agent\"\n81\t\t\"github.com/bborbe/errors\"\n82\t\t\"github.com/golang/glog\"\n83\t\t\"gopkg.in/yaml.v3\"\n84\t)\n85\t\n86\t// extractFrontmatter returns the YAML frontmatter block between the leading\n87\t// \"---\" and the closing \"\\n---\" delimiters. Ported from the controller's\n88\t// pkg/scanner/frontmatter.go (spec 005 — the reconcile loop reads vault task\n89\t// files through git-rest and needs the same parsing the controller uses).\n90\tfunc extractFrontmatter(ctx context.Context, content []byte) (string, error) {\n91\t\ts := string(content)\n92\t\tconst delim = \"---\"\n93\t\tif !strings.HasPrefix(s, delim) {\n94\t\t\treturn \"\", errors.Errorf(ctx, \"no frontmatter delimiter found\")\n95\t\t}\n96\t\trest := strings.TrimPrefix(s, delim)\n97\t\tif strings.HasPrefix(rest, \"\\r\\n\") {\n98\t\t\trest = rest[2:]\n99\t\t} else if strings.HasPrefix(rest, \"\\n\") {\n100\t\t\trest = rest[1:]\n101\t\t}\n102\t\tidx := strings.Index(rest, \"\\n---\")\n103\t\tif idx == -1 {\n104\t\t\treturn \"\", errors.Errorf(ctx, \"frontmatter not closed\")\n105\t\t}\n106\t\treturn rest[:idx], nil\n107\t}\n108\t\n109\t// extractBody returns the markdown body after the closing frontmatter delimiter.\n110\tfunc extractBody(content []byte) string {\n111\t\ts := string(content)\n112\t\tconst delim = \"---\"\n113\t\tif !strings.HasPrefix(s, delim) {\n114\t\t\treturn s\n115\t\t}\n116\t\trest := strings.TrimPrefix(s, delim)\n117\t\tif strings.HasPrefix(rest, \"\\r\\n\") {\n118\t\t\trest = rest[2:]\n119\t\t} else if strings.HasPrefix(rest, \"\\n\") {\n120\t\t\trest = rest[1:]\n121\t\t}\n122\t\tidx := strings.Index(rest, \"\\n---\")\n123\t\tif idx == -1 {\n124\t\t\treturn s\n125\t\t}\n126\t\tafter := rest[idx+4:] // skip \"\\n---\"\n127\t\tif strings.HasPrefix(after, \"\\r\\n\") {\n128\t\t\tafter = after[2:]\n129\t\t} else if strings.HasPrefix(after, \"\\n\") {\n130\t\t\tafter = after[1:]\n131\t\t}\n132\t\treturn after\n133\t}\n134\t\n135\t// parseTaskFile parses a vault task file into a lib.Task. ok=false when the\n136\t// file has no valid frontmatter or no task_identifier (the file is not a task\n137\t// the executor can drive). The Content is the markdown body — it is preserved\n138\t// verbatim because SpawnJob renders it into the spawned Job's TASK_CONTENT env\n139\t// (renderTaskContent in pkg/spawner), so a dropped body would spawn an agent\n140\t// with no instructions.\n141\tfunc parseTaskFile(ctx context.Context, content []byte) (lib.Task, bool) {"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b68d74ad5231f9ea","session_id":"3667b84f-c892-4ca5-8115-a830204bf3b3","uuid":"118cbfe3-bb82-4ba7-a549-f3a3e853c6ed","timestamp":"2026-09-03T18:07:28.791Z","subagent_type":"dark-factory:prompt-creator","task_description":"Generate prompts from spec 005"}
