{"type":"system","subtype":"task_notification","task_id":"a8517317a53f981d8","tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b68d74ad5231f9ea","status":"completed","output_file":"/tmp/claude-1000/-workspace/3667b84f-c892-4ca5-8115-a830204bf3b3/tasks/a8517317a53f981d8.output","summary":"All four prompts are complete and internally consistent. Here is the summary.\n\n## Files created\n\nAll in the inbox `/workspace/prompts/` (relative to repo root — the docker mount is `/workspace`):\n\n- `/workspace/prompts/1-spec-005-gitrest-client.md` — read-only git-rest client package (`List`/`Get`/`IsReady` + gateway-secret auth), `ReadGitRestGatewaySecret` (reads the secret value from K8s by NAME, data key `gateway-secret`), the 3 env config fields (`GITREST_URL`, `GITREST_GATEWAY_SECRET`, `TASK_GLOB`), the `FakeGitRestClient` counterfeiter mock, full httptest + fake-clientset tests.\n- `/workspace/prompts/2-spec-005-reconcile-loop.md` — the core feature: `ReconcileOnce`/`RunReconcileLoop` on `taskEventHandler`, `defaultReconcileIntervalSeconds = 60s` + `reconcilePassTimeout = 30s` package constants, eligibility filter via a new `pkg/handler/task_file.go` (ported frontmatter/body parsing), `executor_reconcile_redriven_total` counter, main.go/factory wiring, `## Unreleased` `feat:` bullet, and a NEW `pkg/handler/task_reconcile_test.go` covering ACs 1–4 + 6 and every failure-mode row.\n- `/workspace/prompts/3-spec-005-spawn-lock.md` — unconditional per-assignee lock in `spawnIfNeeded` + the concurrent reconcile-vs-Kafka double-spawn regression test (AC 5).\n- `/workspace/prompts/4-spec-005-readme-doc.md` — README docs for the three env vars (documentation-only).\n\n## Execution order\n\n`1 → 2 → 3 → 4` (numbered prefixes), matching the spec's Suggested Decomposition row order. Deviation from the decomposition's dependency column, flagged for the reviewer: **prompt 3 depends on prompt 2** for its regression test, because AC 5's evidence explicitly races \"the two paths\" (reconcile + Kafka), so `ReconcileOnce` must exist first.\n\n## Key decisions\n\n- **Git-rest client is inlined verbatim in prompt 1** (read-only subset, no `Post`/`Delete`, no retry/backoff, no metrics). Rationale: `agent-task-controller` is not a go.mod dependency and may not be in the container's module cache; the rules say never to add a cross-repo import, so the port is self-contained.\n- **Gateway secret by NAME**: `GITREST_GATEWAY_SECRET` holds a K8s Secret NAME (the `JobKafkaClientCertSecret` pattern per spec Security); the executor reads the value at startup and holds it in memory only. The data key `gateway-secret` is verified against the `bborbe/agent` helm templates, so it is not invented. **Deployment dependency flagged**: the executor ServiceAccount currently has no `secrets: get` permission (verified in the chart's `executor-rbac.yaml`) — the chart-side RBAC grant and env wiring are operator-ladder work, surfaced in prompt 4's README and in this report.\n- **Reconcile eligibility uses the DEFAULT trigger sets** (status `in_progress`; phase `{planning, execution, ai_review}`), not per-Config trigger overrides — matching AC 1's literal wording and keeping the loop a baseline floor. Added as a reviewer decision note in prompt 2's context.\n- **Env fields declared in prompt 1, consumed in prompt 2** (per the decomposition's \"executor env wiring\" row); the fields are arg-parse surface until prompt 2 lands.\n- **Task body preserved verbatim** in `parseTaskFile` — `SpawnJob` renders `TASK_CONTENT` from `task.Content`, so a dropped body would spawn an agent with no instructions.\n- **`-mod=mod` everywhere** (repo has no vendor dir; `make test` uses `-mod=mod`).\n- **No scenario prompt**: the reconcile loop is fully unit-testable with fake git-rest + fake spawner (scenario condition (a) fails), so the 4 implementation prompts suffice — consistent with the spec's decomposition.\n\n## Constraints repeated per prompt\n\nFrozen repo conventions (Ginkgo/Gomega v2, `bborbe/errors`, counterfe