{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bc5f3bc160457628","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tstatus: draft\n3\tspec: [005-bug-executor-restart-drops-deferred-respawn-queue]\n4\tcreated: \"2026-09-03T18:04:37Z\"\n5\tbranch: dark-factory/bug-executor-restart-drops-deferred-respawn-queue\n6\t---\n7\t\n8\t<summary>\n9\t- The executor gains a read-only git-rest HTTP client (`List` / `Get` / `IsReady`) so a future reconcile loop can read vault task files without a vault mount or filesystem view — the same client shape `agent-task-controller` already uses, ported into this repo with no cross-repo import.\n10\t- The ported client sends git-rest's `X-Gateway-Secret` / `X-Gateway-Initator` auth headers when a gateway secret is configured; with no secret it sends no headers, so auth-disabled git-rest still works.\n11\t- The gateway secret is referenced by K8s secret NAME (the `JobKafkaClientCertSecret` pattern), never the value in env: a new helper reads the secret's `gateway-secret` data key from the K8s API and returns the value for the client to use in-memory only.\n12\t- Three new executor env config values are declared on the `application` struct — `GITREST_URL`, `GITREST_GATEWAY_SECRET` (secret name, default empty = no auth), `TASK_GLOB` (default `24 Tasks/*.md`) — so the config surface is fixed before the reconcile loop prompt consumes them.\n13\t- A counterfeiter mock (`FakeGitRestClient`) is generated so downstream prompts can test against a fake vault source.\n14\t- Full HTTP-level tests (httptest) cover success, 503-readiness, error, and auth-header paths for all three methods; the secret-read helper is tested against a fake clientset.\n15\t</summary>\n16\t\n17\t<objective>\n18\tEstablish the executor's vault-read contract: a small, read-only git-rest HTTP client (`List`/`Get`/`IsReady`) with gateway-secret auth, plus the three executor env config values it is configured from, so the reconcile loop built in the next prompt can derive task state from the vault without a vault mount or filesystem view.\n19\t</objective>\n20\t\n21\t<context>\n22\tRead `/home/node/.claude/CLAUDE.md` for project conventions (Ginkgo/Gomega v2, `github.com/bborbe/errors` wrapping, counterfeiter mocks, glog V(n) gating, coverage ≥80% for new code).\n23\t\n24\tRead these files fully before changing anything:\n25\t- `/workspace/main.go` — the `application` struct (lines 42-65) shows the exact field-tag pattern for new env config (`required:\"false\" arg:\"...\" env:\"...\" usage:\"...\" default:\"...\"`). Mirror it.\n26\t- `/workspace/pkg/metrics/metrics_test.go` and `/workspace/pkg/metrics/metrics_suite_test.go` — the Ginkgo suite-file pattern to mirror for the new `pkg/gitrestclient` package.\n27\t- `/workspace/pkg/spawner/job_spawner.go` (lines 36-37) — the `//counterfeiter:generate -o ../../mocks/...` annotation format to copy for the new interface.\n28\t- `/workspace/pkg/job_watcher_internal_test.go` (lines 19-21) — the `k8s.io/client-go/kubernetes/fake` `fake.NewSimpleClientset(...)` pattern for the secret-read helper test.\n29\t- `/workspace/pkg/config_resolver.go` (lines 18-20) — how `github.com/bborbe/errors` `errors.Errorf(ctx, ...)` / `errors.Wrapf(ctx, err, ...)` are used for config-resolution errors, matching the error style required here.\n30\t\n31\tReference for the ported client shape (read-only subset): the controller's client at `/home/node/go/pkg/mod/github.com/bborbe/agent-task-controller@v0.6.6/pkg/gitrestclient/git_rest_client.go` — `Get`, `List`, `IsReady`, `fileURL`, `setAuthHeaders`. The executor port drops `Post`/`PostIfAbsent`/`Delete`, the retry/backoff (reads fail-fast), and the metrics dependency (spec 005 Security: \"git-rest reads are read-only (`List`/`Get`); the executor never writes vault files through git-rest\"). If that module is not present in the container's module cache, the target code below is authoritative — do not add `agent-task-controller` to go.mod.\n32\t\n33\tThe git-rest auth contract (from the controller's client, do NOT alter the header names):\n34\t- `X-Gateway-Secret` — the shared secret value (exact string match).\n35\t- `X-Gateway-Initator` — caller identity (deliberate misspelling, do NOT change to \"Initiator\"). This executor sends `agent-task-executor`.\n36\t- `/readiness` returns 200 when ready and 503 while unavailable; 503 is a valid not-ready state, not an error.\n37\t\n38\tDecision note for the reviewer: the env var names `GITREST_URL` / `GITREST_GATEWAY_SECRET` / `TASK_GLOB` and the Secret data key `gateway-secret` are chosen to match the controller's chart conventions (verified in the `github.com/bborbe/agent` helm templates: `controller.gatewaySecret` chart-created Secret data key `gateway-secret`, consumed via `secretKeyRef`). The chart-side wiring of these names (and the executor ServiceAccount `secrets: get` grant) is operator-ladder work outside this repo — flagged, not executed here.\n39\t\n40\tRelevant docs (in-container paths):\n41\t- `/home/node/.claude/plugins/marketplaces/coding/docs/go-testing-guide.md` — Ginkgo/Gomega, external test packages, coverage ≥80%.\n42\t- `/home/node/.claude/plugins/marketplaces/coding/docs/go-error-wrapping-guide.md` — `github.com/bborbe/errors`, never `fmt.Errorf`.\n43\t- `/home/node/.claude/plugins/marketplaces/coding/docs/go-security-linting.md` — gosec rules for the HTTP client (30s timeout, 10 MiB read cap are carried over from the controller and already lint-clean).\n44\t- `/home/node/.claude/plugins/marketplaces/coding/docs/definition-of-done.md` — coverage rules for new code.\n45\t</context>\n46\t\n47\t<requirements>\n48\t1. Create the new package directory `/workspace/pkg/gitrestclient/` and the file `/workspace/pkg/gitrestclient/git_rest_client.go` with the following content verbatim (this is the ported read-only subset of the controller's client, minus metrics/backoff/writes). Keep the BSD license header:\n49\t\n50\t```go\n51\t// Copyright (c) 2026 Benjamin Borbe All rights reserved.\n52\t// Use of this source code is governed by a BSD-style\n53\t// license that can be found in the LICENSE file.\n54\t\n55\tpackage gitrestclient\n56\t\n57\timport (\n58\t\t\"context\"\n59\t\t\"encoding/json\"\n60\t\t\"io\"\n61\t\t\"net/http\"\n62\t\t\"net/url\"\n63\t\t\"strings\"\n64\t\t\"time\"\n65\t\n66\t\t\"github.com/bborbe/errors\"\n67\t)\n68\t\n69\t//counterfeiter:generate -o ../../mocks/git_rest_client.go --fake-name FakeGitRestClient . GitRestClient\n70\t\n71\t// GitRestClient is the HTTP client for git-rest's /api/v1/files REST API.\n72\t// All paths are relative to the repo root (e.g. \"tasks/foo.md\"). The executor\n73\t// uses only the read surface (List/Get/IsReady) — it never writes vault files\n74\t// through git-rest (spec 005 Security).\n75\ttype GitRestClient interface {\n76\t\t// Get retrieves the current content of the file at relPath.\n77\t\tGet(ctx context.Context, relPath string) ([]byte, error)\n78\t\t// List returns relative paths matching the single-level glob pattern (e.g. \"tasks/*.md\").\n79\t\tList(ctx context.Context, glob string) ([]string, error)\n80\t\t// IsReady reports whether git-rest's /readiness returns 200.\n81\t\t// Returns (false, nil) when git-rest returns 503 — that is a valid not-ready state, not an error.\n82\t\t// Returns (false, err) only on network failure or unexpected response.\n83\t\tIsReady(ctx context.Context) (bool, error)\n84\t}\n85\t\n86\t// NewGitRestClient creates a GitRestClient targeting the git-rest instance at\n87\t// baseURL. gatewaySecret is the shared secret enforced by git-rest's\n88\t// gateway-secret auth; when empty, no auth headers are sent (backward-compat\n89\t// with auth-disabled git-rest). gatewayInitiator is the caller identity logged\n90\t// by git-rest on auth failure (pass a stable value, e.g. \"agent-task-executor\").\n91\tfunc NewGitRestClient(baseURL, gatewaySecret, gatewayInitiator string) GitRestClient {\n92\t\treturn &gitRestClient{\n93\t\t\tbaseURL:          strings.TrimRight(baseURL, \"/\"),\n94\t\t\thttpClient:       &http.Client{Timeout: 30 * time.Second},\n95\t\t\tgatewaySecret:    gatewaySecret,\n96\t\t\tgatewayInitiator: gatewayInitiator,\n97\t\t}\n98\t}\n99\t\n100\ttype gitRestClient struct {\n101\t\tbaseURL          string\n102\t\thttpClient       *http.Client\n103\t\tgatewaySecret    string\n104\t\tgatewayInitiator string\n105\t}\n106\t\n107\t// setAuthHeaders sets the gateway-secret auth headers on req when the secret is configured.\n108\t// No-op when gatewaySecret is empty — keeps backward compatibility with auth-disabled git-rest.\n109\t//\n110\t// Header names are part of the git-rest public contract (spec 004) — do NOT alter:\n111\t//\n112\t//\tX-Gateway-Secret   — the shared secret\n113\t//\tX-Gateway-Initator — caller identity (deliberate misspelling, do NOT change to \"Initiator\")\n114\tfunc (g *gitRestClient) setAuthHeaders(req *http.Request) {\n115\t\tif g.gatewaySecret == \"\" {\n116\t\t\treturn\n117\t\t}\n118\t\treq.Header.Set(\"X-Gateway-Secret\", g.gatewaySecret)\n119\t\treq.Header.Set(\"X-Gateway-Initator\", g.gatewayInitiator)\n120\t}\n121\t\n122\t// fileURL builds /api/v1/files/<relPath> with proper percent-escaping so\n123\t// characters like %, space, # in relPath survive the round-trip to git-rest.\n124\tfunc (g *gitRestClient) fileURL(relPath string) string {\n125\t\tsegments := strings.Split(relPath, \"/\")\n126\t\tfor i, s := range segments {\n127\t\t\tsegments[i] = url.PathEscape(s)\n128\t\t}\n129\t\treturn g.baseURL + \"/api/v1/files/\" + strings.Join(segments, \"/\")\n130\t}\n131\t\n132\t// Get retrieves file content from git-rest. Does not retry — reads fail-fast.\n133\tfunc (g *gitRestClient) Get(ctx context.Context, relPath string) ([]byte, error) {\n134\t\treqURL := g.fileURL(relPath)\n135\t\treq, err := http.NewRequestWithContext(ctx, http.MethodGet, reqURL, nil)\n136\t\tif err != nil {\n137\t\t\treturn nil, errors.Wrapf(ctx, err, \"create GET request for %s\", relPath)\n138\t\t}\n139\t\tg.setAuthHeaders(req)\n140\t\tresp, err := g.httpClient.Do(req)\n141\t\tif err != nil {\n142\t\t\treturn nil, errors.Wrapf(ctx, err, \"GET %s\", relPath)\n143\t\t}\n144\t\tdefer resp.Body.Close()\n145\t\tbody, err := io.ReadAll(io.LimitReader(resp.Body, 10*1024*1024)) // 10 MiB max\n146\t\tif err != nil {\n147\t\t\treturn nil, errors.Wrapf(ctx, err, \"read GET response body for %s\", relPath)\n148\t\t}\n149\t\tif resp.StatusCode != http.StatusOK {\n150\t\t\tpreview := string(body)\n151\t\t\tif len(preview) > 100 {\n152\t\t\t\tpreview = preview[:100]\n153\t\t\t}\n154\t\t\treturn nil, errors.Errorf(ctx, \"GET %s returned %d: %s\", relPath, resp.StatusCode, preview)\n155\t\t}\n156\t\treturn body, nil\n157\t}\n158\t\n159\t// List returns paths matching the glob pattern. Does not retry — reads fail-fast.\n160\tfunc (g *gitRestClient) List(ctx context.Context, glob string) ([]string, error) {\n161\t\treqURL := g.baseURL + \"/api/v1/files/\"\n162\t\treq, err := http.NewRequestWithContext(ctx, http.MethodGet, reqURL, nil)\n163\t\tif err != nil {\n164\t\t\treturn nil, errors.Wrapf(ctx, err, \"create LIST request for glob %s\", glob)\n165\t\t}\n166\t\tq := url.Values{}\n167\t\tq.Set(\"glob\", glob)\n168\t\treq.URL.RawQuery = q.Encode()\n169\t\tg.setAuthHeaders(req)\n170\t\tresp, err := g.httpClient.Do(req)\n171\t\tif err != nil {\n172\t\t\treturn nil, errors.Wrapf(ctx, err, \"LIST glob %s\", glob)\n173\t\t}\n174\t\tdefer resp.Body.Close()\n175\t\tbody, err := io.ReadAll(io.LimitReader(resp.Body, 10*1024*1024)) // 10 MiB max\n176\t\tif err != nil {\n177\t\t\treturn nil, errors.Wrapf(ctx, err, \"read LIST response body for glob %s\", glob)\n178\t\t}\n179\t\tif resp.StatusCode != http.StatusOK {\n180\t\t\tpreview := string(body)\n181\t\t\tif len(preview) > 100 {\n182\t\t\t\tpreview = preview[:100]\n183\t\t\t}\n184\t\t\treturn nil, errors.Errorf(ctx, \"LIST glob %s returned %d: %s\", glob, resp.StatusCode, preview)\n185\t\t}\n186\t\tvar paths []string\n187\t\tif err := json.Unmarshal(body, &paths); err != nil {\n188\t\t\treturn nil, errors.Wrapf(ctx, err, \"parse LIST response for glob %s\", glob)\n189\t\t}\n190\t\treturn paths, nil\n191\t}\n192\t\n193\t// IsReady checks git-rest's /readiness endpoint.\n194\tfunc (g *gitRestClient) IsReady(ctx context.Context) (bool, error) {\n195\t\treqURL := g.baseURL + \"/readiness\"\n196\t\treq, err := http.NewRequestWithContext(ctx, http.MethodGet, reqURL, nil)\n197\t\tif err != nil {\n198\t\t\treturn false, errors.Wrapf(ctx, err, \"create readiness request\")\n199\t\t}\n200\t\tresp, err := g.httpClient.Do(req)\n201\t\tif err != nil {\n202\t\t\treturn false, errors.Wrapf(ctx, err, \"readiness check\")\n203\t\t}\n204\t\t_, _ = io.Copy(io.Discard, resp.Body)\n205\t\t_ = resp.Body.Close()\n206\t\tswitch resp.StatusCode {\n207\t\tcase http.StatusOK:\n208\t\t\treturn true, nil\n209\t\tcase http.StatusServiceUnavailable:\n210\t\t\treturn false, nil\n211\t\tdefault:\n212\t\t\treturn false, errors.Errorf(ctx, \"readiness returned unexpected status %d\", resp.StatusCode)\n213\t\t}\n214\t}\n215\t```\n216\t\n217\tDo NOT add any other methods, metrics, or retry logic — the executor is a read-only consumer of git-rest (YAGNI; the spec's observability for this feature is the reconcile-loop log line + counter in the next prompt, not per-call git-rest metrics).\n218\t\n219\t2. Create `/workspace/pkg/gitrestclient/gitrestclient_suite_test.go` in `package gitrestclient_test` mirroring the pattern in `/workspace/pkg/metrics/metrics_suite_test.go`, including the counterfeiter go:generate directive (copy the exact directive line from `/workspace/pkg/handler/task_event_handler_test.go:7`):\n220\t```go\n221\t//go:generate go run github.com/maxbrunsfeld/counterfeiter/v6@v6.12.2 -generate\n222\t```\n223\tIt must contain `func TestGitRestClient(t *testing.T)` calling `RegisterFailHandler(Fail)` and `RunSpecs(t, \"GitRestClient Suite\")`.\n224\t\n225\t3. Create `/workspace/pkg/gitrestclient/git_rest_client_test.go` in `package gitrestclient_test` using `net/http/httptest` servers (mirror the assertion style of the controller's `git_rest_client_test.go`: the handler asserts `r.Method`, `r.URL.Path`, and `r.URL.Query()` on each request). Cover:\n226\t   a. `Get` 200: returns the exact body bytes; handler asserts method GET and path `/api/v1/files/tasks/foo.md`.\n227\t   b. `Get` non-200 (404): returns an error whose message contains the status code.\n228\t   c. `Get` with a gateway secret configured: handler asserts `X-Gateway-Secret` and `X-Gateway-Initator` headers are present with the configured values, then returns 200.\n229\t   d. `Get` with empty gateway secret: handler asserts NEITHER auth header is present, then returns 200.\n230\t   e. `Get` path escaping: relPath `\"24 Tasks/a b.md\"` produces a request whose `r.URL.Path` contains the escaped segments (space and the path segment separators survive as separate path elements — assert the handler receives a 2-element path `\"/api/v1/files/24 Tasks/a b.md\"` decoded; `url.PathEscape` escapes the space in the URL, so assert on `r.URL.EscapedPath()` containing `%20`).\n231\t   f. `List` 200: handler asserts the query parameter `glob` equals the configured glob, returns JSON `[\"24 Tasks/a.md\",\"24 Tasks/b.md\"]`; client returns exactly those two strings.\n232\t   g. `List` non-200: returns an error containing the status code.\n233\t   h. `List` with unparseable body (`not json`): returns an error (no panic).\n234\t   i. `IsReady` 200: returns `(true, nil)`.\n235\t   j. `IsReady` 503: returns `(false, nil)` — a valid not-ready state, NOT an error.\n236\t   k. `IsReady` 500: returns `(false, err)`.\n237\t   l. `IsReady` against a closed server (`server.Close()` before the call): returns `(false, err)` — network failure path.\n238\t\n239\t4. Create `/workspace/pkg/gitrest_gateway_secret.go` in `/workspace/pkg/` (package `pkg`) with:\n240\t```go\n241\t// Copyright (c) 2026 Benjamin Borbe All rights reserved.\n242\t// Use of this source code is governed by a BSD-style\n243\t// license that can be found in the LICENSE file.\n244\t\n245\tpackage pkg\n246\t\n247\timport (\n248\t\t\"context\"\n249\t\n250\t\t\"github.com/bborbe/errors\"\n251\t\tlibk8s \"github.com/bborbe/k8s\"\n252\t\tmetav1 \"k8s.io/apimachinery/pkg/apis/meta/v1\"\n253\t\t\"k8s.io/client-go/kubernetes\"\n254\t)\n255\t\n256\t// gitRestGatewaySecretDataKey is the data key inside the referenced K8s Secret\n257\t// that holds the git-rest gateway secret value. Matches the controller chart's\n258\t// `gateway-secret` data key (the Secret git-rest and the controller share).\n259\tconst gitRestGatewaySecretDataKey = \"gateway-secret\"\n260\t\n261\t// ReadGitRestGatewaySecret returns the git-rest gateway secret value from the\n262\t// named K8s Secret, or \"\" when secretName is empty (gateway auth disabled).\n263\t// The value is read once at startup and held in memory only — it is never\n264\t// logged, never embedded in the image, and never in env (spec 005 Security;\n265\t// the env var GITREST_GATEWAY_SECRET references the secret by NAME, matching\n266\t// the JobKafkaClientCertSecret pattern). Returns an error when the Secret is\n267\t// missing or lacks the gateway-secret data key, so a misconfigured deployment\n268\t// fails loudly at startup instead of silently sending no auth header.\n269\tfunc ReadGitRestGatewaySecret(\n270\t\tctx context.Context,\n271\t\tkubeClient kubernetes.Interface,\n272\t\tnamespace libk8s.Namespace,\n273\t\tsecretName string,\n274\t) (string, error) {\n275\t\tif secretName == \"\" {\n276\t\t\treturn \"\", nil\n277\t\t}\n278\t\tsecret, err := kubeClient.CoreV1().Secrets(namespace.String()).Get(ctx, secretName, metav1.GetOptions{})\n279\t\tif err != nil {\n280\t\t\treturn \"\", errors.Wrapf(ctx, err, \"get git-rest gateway secret %q\", secretName)\n281\t\t}\n282\t\tvalue, ok := secret.Data[gitRestGatewaySecretDataKey]\n283\t\tif !ok {\n284\t\t\treturn \"\", errors.Errorf(ctx, \"secret %q lacks data key %q\", secretName, gitRestGatewaySecretDataKey)\n285\t\t}\n286\t\treturn string(value), nil\n287\t}\n288\t```\n289\tThis function has no counterfeiter annotation — callers pass the real `kubernetes.Interface` and tests use the fake clientset.\n290\t\n291\t5. Create `/workspace/pkg/gitrest_gateway_secret_test.go` in `package pkg_test` (this registers into the existing \"Pkg Suite\" launched by `TestPkg` in `/workspace/pkg/agent_configuration_test.go`). Use `fake.NewSimpleClientset(&corev1.Secret{ObjectMeta: metav1.ObjectMeta{Name: \"gw-secret\", Namespace: \"test-ns\"}, Data: map[string][]byte{\"gateway-secret\": []byte(\"s3cret\")}})` (imports `k8s.io/client-go/kubernetes/fake`, `corev1 \"k8s.io/api/core/v1\"`, `metav1 \"k8s.io/apimachinery/pkg/apis/meta/v1\"`). Cover:\n292\t   a. empty secretName → `(\"\", nil)` — auth disabled.\n293\t   b. secret present with `gateway-secret` data key → returns the value `\"s3cret\"`.\n294\t   c. secret missing (fake clientset without the secret) → returns an error mentioning the secret name.\n295\t   d. secret present WITHOUT the `gateway-secret` data key (e.g. `Data: map[string][]byte{\"other\": []byte(\"x\")}`) → returns an error mentioning the data key.\n296\t\n297\t6. Add three new env config fields to the `application` struct in `/workspace/main.go`. Place them directly after the `JobKafkaCaCertSecret` field (line 64), preserving the existing field-tag alignment style:\n298\t```go\n299\t\t// GitRestURL is the git-rest HTTP API base URL the reconcile loop reads the\n300\t\t// vault through. Matches the controller's default git-rest service address.\n301\t\t// Consumed by the reconcile loop in the follow-up prompt.\n302\t\tGitRestURL string `required:\"false\" arg:\"git-rest-url\" env:\"GITREST_URL\" usage:\"git-rest HTTP API base URL the reconcile loop reads vault task files through\" default:\"http://vault-obsidian-openclaw:9090\"`\n303\t\t// GitRestGatewaySecret holds the NAME of the K8s Secret carrying the\n304\t\t// git-rest gateway secret (data key `gateway-secret`) — not the secret\n305\t\t// value itself. Same resource-reference pattern as JobKafkaClientCertSecret:\n306\t\t// a name, not secret material, so nothing secret-shaped enters the image or\n307\t\t// the Deployment manifest. Consumed by the reconcile loop in the follow-up\n308\t\t// prompt.\n309\t\tGitRestGatewaySecret string `required:\"false\" arg:\"git-rest-gateway-secret\" env:\"GITREST_GATEWAY_SECRET\" usage:\"Name of the existing K8s secret holding the git-rest gateway secret (data key gateway-secret); empty disables gateway auth\"`\n310\t\t// TaskGlob is the git-rest single-level glob selecting the vault task files\n311\t\t// the reconcile loop evaluates, relative to the repo root. Consumed by the\n312\t\t// reconcile loop in the follow-up prompt.\n313\t\tTaskGlob string `required:\"false\" arg:\"task-glob\" env:\"TASK_GLOB\" usage:\"git-rest glob selecting vault task files to reconcile\" default:\"24 Tasks/*.md\"`\n314\t```\n315\tDo NOT wire these values anywhere in this prompt — the reconcile loop that consumes them is the next prompt. They exist here to fix the config surface (names, defaults) before the consumer lands.\n316\t\n317\t7. Regenerate the mock: run `go generate -mod=mod ./pkg/gitrestclient/...` (or `go generate -mod=mod ./...`) so `/workspace/mocks/git_rest_client.go` with `FakeGitRestClient` is produced from the `//counterfeiter:generate` annotation in requirement 1. The mock must satisfy `gitrestclient.GitRestClient` (methods `Get`, `List`, `IsReady` with the usual counterfeiter `...Returns`, `...CallCount`, `...ArgsForCall` accessors). Do not hand-write the mock.\n318\t\n319\t8. Do NOT add a CHANGELOG entry in this prompt — the feature-level `feat:` bullet covering the whole reconcile feature lands in the next prompt, and dark-factory reads the prefix from that single entry for the version bump.\n320\t</requirements>\n321\t\n322\t<constraints>\n323\t- Repo conventions are frozen: Ginkgo/Gomega v2 tests (no stdlib table tests), `github.com/bborbe/errors` wrapping (never `fmt.Errorf`), counterfeiter mocks for any new dependency (`//counterfeiter:generate`), glog `V(n)` gating.\n324\t- The executor does NOT gain a vault mount or filesystem view; the vault is read only through git-rest. This prompt ships the read-only client; it must NOT add any write method (`Post`/`PostIfAbsent`/`Delete`) or any retry/backoff — reads fail-fast, matching the controller's read behavior.\n325\t- The git-rest auth header names `X-Gateway-Secret` and `X-Gateway-Initator` (deliberate misspelling) are part of the public git-rest contract — do NOT alter them.\n326\t- `GITREST_GATEWAY_SECRET` holds a K8s Secret NAME (like `JOB_KAFKA_CLIENT_CERT_SECRET`), never the secret value; the value is read from the K8s API and held in memory only.\n327\t- Do NOT add `github.com/bborbe/agent-task-controller` to go.mod — the client is ported in, not imported.\n328\t- Do NOT wire the Helm chart or config-repo values — out of scope (the chart lives outside this repo; the deploy surface is the spec's operator ladder).\n329\t- Do NOT commit — dark-factory handles git.\n330\t- Existing tests must still pass.\n331\t</constraints>\n332\t\n333\t<verification>\n334\tRun `go test -mod=mod ./pkg/gitrestclient/... ./pkg/` iteratively after each change (fast feedback loop), then `make precommit` ONCE at the very end.\n335\t\n336\t- `go test -mod=mod ./pkg/gitrestclient/...` — exits 0.\n337\t- `go test -mod=mod ./pkg/` — exits 0 (the new secret-read test registers into the Pkg Suite).\n338\t- `make precommit` — exits 0 (runs counterfeiter via `go generate -mod=mod ./...`; the new mock must be produced and committed by dark-factory).\n339\t- `ls mocks/git_rest_client.go` — the FakeGitRestClient mock exists.\n340\t- `grep -n 'GITREST_URL\\|GITREST_GATEWAY_SECRET\\|TASK_GLOB' main.go` — returns ≥1 line each (acceptance-criterion evidence for the env wiring).\n341\t- `grep -rn 'func (g \\*gitRestClient) List\\|func (g \\*gitRestClient) Get\\|func (g \\*gitRestClient) IsReady' pkg/gitrestclient/` — all three read methods present.\n342\t- `go test -mod=mod -coverprofile=/tmp/cover.out ./pkg/gitrestclient/... && go tool cover -func=/tmp/cover.out` — confirm `Get`, `List`, `IsReady`, `fileURL`, `setAuthHeaders` and `pkg.ReadGitRestGatewaySecret` are each exercised by at least one test (≥80% statement coverage for new code).\n343\t\n344\tDo NOT run `docker`, `make build`, `kubectl`, `dark-factory`, `gh`, or `scripts/*.sh` commands in this prompt — those are operator-executable and belong on the spec's verification ladder.\n345\t</verification>\n346\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ade17fd4b63e6ead","session_id":"3667b84f-c892-4ca5-8115-a830204bf3b3","uuid":"2191c514-60a5-422a-b10f-4186a49cae07","timestamp":"2026-09-03T18:08:19.554Z","subagent_type":"dark-factory:prompt-auditor","task_description":"Audit prompt 1 gitrest-client"}
