{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-be98c83e9fd2dcf3","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Agent Task Executor\n2\t\n3\tKafka event consumer + Kubernetes **Job spawner** for the\n4\t[bborbe/agent](https://github.com/bborbe/agent) task system. It consumes\n5\t`task.CreateCommand` events, matches each task's `assignee` to a registered agent\n6\t`Config` CR (`agent.benjamin-borbe.de/v1`), and spawns one Kubernetes Job per\n7\ttask/phase using that agent's image, env, resources and secrets — propagating\n8\t`BRANCH` / `TOPIC_PREFIX` to the child Job.\n9\t\n10\tImage tags: an agent `Config.spec.image` that already carries a tag (a semver\n11\tpin, e.g. `…/agent-claude:v0.1.1`) is used as-is; an **untagged** image gets the\n12\trunning branch appended (`…/agent-backtest` → `…/agent-backtest:dev`). Deployed\n13\tvia the `agent` Helm chart; published image `docker.io/bborbe/agent-task-executor`.\n14\t\n15\t## Links\n16\t\n17\tDev:\n18\thttps://dev.quant.benjamin-borbe.de/admin/agent-task-executor/setloglevel/3\n19\thttps://dev.quant.benjamin-borbe.de/admin/agent-task-executor/agents\n20\thttps://dev.quant.benjamin-borbe.de/admin/agent-task-executor/healthcheck-trigger\n21\t\n22\tProd:\n23\thttps://prod.quant.benjamin-borbe.de/admin/agent-task-executor/setloglevel/3\n24\thttps://prod.quant.benjamin-borbe.de/admin/agent-task-executor/agents\n25\thttps://prod.quant.benjamin-borbe.de/admin/agent-task-executor/healthcheck-trigger\n26\t\n27\t## License\n28\t\n29\tThis project is licensed under the BSD-style license. See the [LICENSE](LICENSE) file for details.\n30\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-82d8c962a4bd571f","session_id":"3667b84f-c892-4ca5-8115-a830204bf3b3","uuid":"1200b74a-079e-4fbe-b1fd-0ab33d8e1df8","timestamp":"2026-09-03T18:08:21.404Z","subagent_type":"dark-factory:prompt-auditor","task_description":"Audit prompt 4 readme-doc"}
