ered by (a) and (b) — assert the `executor_reconcile_redriven_total` delta explicitly in both.\n465\t    f. Failure mode — git-rest not ready: `fakeGitRestClient.IsReadyReturns(false, nil)`; run `ReconcileOnce`; assert `fakeGitRestClient.ListCallCount() == 0` and `SpawnJobCallCount() == 0` (pass skipped, next tick retries).\n466\t    g. Failure mode — readiness error: `fakeGitRestClient.IsReadyReturns(false, errors.Errorf(ctx, \"boom\"))`; assert `ListCallCount() == 0` and `SpawnJobCallCount() == 0`.\n467\t    h. Failure mode — List error: `IsReadyReturns(true, nil)`, `ListReturns(nil, errors.Errorf(ctx, \"rate limited\"))`; assert `SpawnJobCallCount() == 0` (pass skipped, no panic).\n468\t    i. Failure mode — Get error for one path: `ListReturns([]string{\"24 Tasks/bad.md\"}, nil)`, `GetReturns(nil, errors.Errorf(ctx, \"boom\"))`; assert `SpawnJobCallCount() == 0` and `ReconcileOnce` returns nil (no crash).\n469\t    j. Startup pass (DB 1): run `RunReconcileLoop` in a short-lived context (`context.WithCancel(ctx)`), with `fakeGitRestClient.ListReturns` set; `Eventually(fakeGitRestClient.ListCallCount).Should(BeNumerically(\">=\", 1))` (the immediate startup pass runs before any ticker fire), then `cancel()` and assert `<-done` is nil. Since the interval is 60s, no ticker tick occurs in the test.\n470\t    k. Per-pass abort (DB 7 / failure-mode \"slow or vault large\"): with `fakeGitRestClient.ListReturns([]string{\"24 Tasks/tid-a.md\"}, nil)` set and an already-cancelled parent context (`cancelCtx, cancel := context.WithCancel(ctx); cancel()`), run `ReconcileOnce(cancelCtx)` and assert it returns nil (the `passCtx.Done()` select aborts the pass; no panic, no `SpawnJob`).\n471\t\n472\t11. Add the CHANGELOG entry in `/workspace/CHANGELOG.md` under the existing `## Unreleased` section (append after the current chore bullet):\n473\t    ```\n474\t    - feat: add a periodic reconcile loop that re-derives running tasks from the vault (via git-rest) and live Jobs, so a task deferred behind `maxConcurrentJobs` whose in-memory deferral was lost across an executor restart resumes without a Kafka event or vault edit; observable via `executor_reconcile_redriven_total` and `event=reconcile*` log lines, with the per-assignee spawn lock taken unconditionally to prevent reconcile/event double-spawns\n475\t    ```\n476\t\n477\t12. Do NOT touch `seedDeferredRespawnsFromStore` (lines 642-672) — it remains as-is; the reconcile loop is the new restart-recovery floor and must not be gated on `deferredRespawns` contents. Do NOT change `deferIfAtConcurrencyCap`, `checkActiveCurrentJob`, or the Kafka event path.\n478\t</requirements>\n479\t\n480\t<constraints>\n481\t- Repo conventions are frozen: Ginkgo/Gomega v2 tests (no stdlib table tests), `github.com/bborbe/errors` wrapping (never `fmt.Errorf`), counterfeiter mocks for any new dependency, glog `V(n)` gating.\n482\t- The reconcile interval is a package constant `defaultReconcileIntervalSeconds = 60 * time.Second` — NO CRD field and NO env override (spec Non-goal).\n483\t- The reconcile loop is the source-of-truth floor: it reads the vault via git-rest and live Jobs via the spawner. It must NOT consult or be gated on the in-memory `deferredRespawns` map or `taskStore` (which a restart wipes).\n484\t- Re-driving an eligible task MUST go through the existing `spawnIfNeeded` path so the concurrency cap, trigger budget, and `current_job` grace-window logic apply identically to event-driven and reconcile-driven spawns. Do NOT duplicate any of that logic in the reconcile code.\n485\t- The reconcile eligibility uses the DEFAULT trigger sets (status `in_progress`, phase `{planning, execution, ai_review}`) plus stage/assignee/config gates, per AC 1 — not per-Config trigger overrides.\n486\t- git-rest unavailability must NEVER crash the executor: pass skipped with a log line, next tick retries, Kafka consumption unaffected.\n487\t- The Kafka event path and `deferIfAtConcurrencyCap`/`checkActiveCurrentJob` behavior are unchanged for event-driven spawns.\n488\t- Do NOT add the unconditional spawn lock in this prompt — that is the next prompt.\n489\t- CHANGELOG: append the single `feat:` bullet to the existing `## Unreleased` section (it already exists at HEAD v0.8.3).\n490\t- Do NOT commit — dark-factory handles git.\n491\t- Existing tests must still pass.\n492\t</constraints>\n493\t\n494\t<verification>\n495\tRun `go test -mod=mod ./pkg/handler/... ./pkg/metrics/...` iteratively after each meaningful change (fast feedback loop), then `make precommit` ONCE at the very end.\n496\t\n497\t- `go test -mod=mod ./pkg/handler/...` — exits 0.\n498\t- `go test -mod=mod ./pkg/metrics/...` — exits 0.\n499\t- `make precommit` — exits 0 (regenerates the `FakeTaskEventHandler` mock for the two new interface methods via `go generate -mod=mod ./...`; also regenerates the git-rest mock).\n500\t- `grep -n 'reconcile' pkg/handler/task_event_handler.go` — returns ≥1 line (acceptance-criterion evidence).\n501\t- `grep -rn 'executor_reconcile_redriven_total' pkg/` — returns ≥1 line (acceptance-criterion evidence).\n502\t- `grep -rn 'event=reconcile_redrive' pkg/handler/` — the per-redrive log line format is present.\n503\t- `grep -n 'RunReconcileLoop' main.go pkg/handler/task_event_handler.go` — the loop is registered in service.Run and defined on the handler.\n504\t- `go test -mod=mod -coverprofile=/tmp/cover.out ./pkg/handler/... && go tool cover -func=/tmp/cover.out` — confirm `ReconcileOnce`, `reconcileTask`, `RunReconcileLoop`, `parseTaskFile`, `extractFrontmatter`, `extractBody` are each exercised by at least one test (≥80% statement coverage for new code).\n505\t\n506\tDo NOT run `docker`, `make build`, `kubectl`, `dark-factory`, `gh`, or `scripts/*.sh` commands in this prompt — those are operator-executable and belong on the spec's verification ladder.\n507\t</verification>\n508\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9be1dac94caaf56f","session_id":"3667b84f-c892-4ca5-8115-a830204b