ts>` numbered and specific — PASS. Two numbered requirements; the exact markdown table is inlined; insertion point pinned (\"after the introductory paragraph, before `## Links`\"); non-negotiable substrings listed.\n- [x] `<constraints>` present — PASS. Documentation-only, exact semantics, \"Do NOT edit the Helm chart\", \"Do NOT commit\", no `make precommit` for a docs-only change (consistent with the container CLAUDE.md rule).\n- [x] `<verification>` present with runnable command — PASS. Five `grep` commands on `README.md` (repo-relative, resolves from container cwd `/workspace`).\n- [x] All paths repo-relative or mount-backed — PASS. `/workspace/README.md` is valid (`$PWD` with `.dark-factory.yaml` is mounted to `/workspace` per `yolo-container-setup.md:131`). `/home/node/.claude/plugins/marketplaces/coding/docs/documentation-guide.md` is the coding-plugin doc path, present in the container (verified present at that path here). No `~/` or host-absolute paths.\n- [x] No bare `git ` commands in `<verification>` when git is masked — PASS. Project config is `workflow: direct`, no `hideGit: true`; and the verification block explicitly forbids `git` (line 66) and uses only `grep`.\n- [x] No operator-only commands in `<verification>` — PASS. Only `grep`; line 66 explicitly forbids `docker`/`make build`/`kubectl`/`dark-factory`/`gh`/`git`.\n- [x] File in `prompts/` inbox (not `prompts/in-progress/`) — PASS.\n- [x] Filename not prefixed with dark-factory global number — PASS. `4-` is the documented single-digit multi-prompt ordering prefix (`^[1-9]-spec-\\d{3}-.*\\.md$`).\n- [x] Filename reflects primary change — PASS. `readme-doc` names the deliverable.\n- [x] Status is `idea` or `draft` — PASS (`draft`). Frontmatter also carries `branch:` — confirmed this is a dark-factory-persisted field (workflows.md:168: \"persisted via `branch:` frontmatter\"), present identically in all four sibling prompts, so it is tool-managed, not a writer error. `spec:` is the canonical full-s