cret value is read from K8s by name at startup\") | Correct |\n| `JOB_KAFKA_CLIENT_CERT_SECRET` precedent | `/workspace/main.go:60,63` (\"a resource reference, not secret-shaped\") | Correct — the \"NAME not value\" pattern the README documents is the real in-repo precedent |\n| ServiceAccount `get`/`secrets: get` grant | `/workspace/prompts/1-spec-005-gitrest-client.md:38` | Correct — documented as chart-side operator work, consistent with this prompt's deferral |\n| `/home/node/.claude/plugins/marketplaces/coding/docs/documentation-guide.md` | exists | Correct (verified present) |\n\nNote: the env vars do not yet exist in the repo source (sibling prompts 1–2 are unexecuted, in the inbox). Prompt 4's contract assertions are accurate against the sibling prompts, and its verification is self-contained (README content only), so there is no stale-reference risk — but see Recommendation 3 for the ordering constraint.\n\n## Coding Guidelines Compliance\n\n| Guideline | File | Status |\n|-----------|------|--------|\n| N/A — no Go code in this prompt | — | Compliant (docs-only; no handlers, factories, error wrapping, or test-pattern surfaces to check) |\n\n## YAGNI Pass (scope-creep detector)\n\n- [x] No opt-out flag for the very behavior the prompt ships — PASS (none).\n- [x] Every config field / threshold / branch demanded by the spec Goal — PASS. The three env vars are the spec's own `Constraints` (\"New executor env config: git-rest base URL, gateway secret ..., and the task directory glob. New env vars are documented in the chart and `README.md`\") and decomposition row 4. No invented knobs.\n- [x] No \"future-proofing\" knobs — PASS.\n\n## Critical Issues\n\nNone.\n\n## Recommendations\n\n1. **Summary bullet count (minor DoD deviation).** The DoD asks for 5–10 bullets; `<summary>` has 4 (lines 9–12). Suggest adding a fifth, e.g.:\n   - Old: `- No Go, YAML, or chart changes — documentation only.`\n   - New: `- No Go, YAML, or chart changes — documentation only; the chart-side env wiring and RBAC grant stay on the operator verification ladder.`\n\n2. **Reference `readme-guide.md` in `<context>`.** `documentation-guide.md` is the general guide; the coding plugin's `readme-guide.md` is the README-specific one (env-var/configuration section guidance) and is the better fit for this edit. Suggest appending to `<context>`:\n   - Old: `- `/home/node/.claude/plugins/marketplaces/coding/docs/documentation-guide.md` — docs conventions.`\n   - New: `- `/home/node/.claude/plugins/marketplaces/coding/docs/documentation-guide.md` — docs conventions.\\n- `/home/node/.claude/plugins/marketplaces/coding/docs/readme-guide.md` — README structure and env-var/configuration section guidance.`\n\n3. **Execution-order note (informational, no change required).** The README documents env vars that only exist in code after prompts 1 and 2 land. The spec's decomposition already encodes the dependency (row 4 \"Depends on: prompt 1\"); this is fine as long as the daemon executes the batch in order. If there is any mechanism that could run prompt 4 standalone, it should be blocked until prompts 1–2 are merged — otherwise the README ships docs for a config surface that does not yet exist in `main.go`.\n\n## Strengths\n\n- Container-autonomy handled correctly and explicitly: the operator-side work (chart env wiring, `EXECUTOR_VERSION`, RBAC grant) is named, scoped to the spec's verification ladder, and refused in the prompt body rather than split into an \"operator steps\" section.\n- Verification is self-contained and container-executable (`grep` on `README.md` only), with a correct explicit prohibition on git/operator commands.\n- The documented contract matches the sibling prompt 1 env declarations verbatim (names, defaults, data key, NAME-not-value semantics), so there is no drift risk between the README and the code that will declare these fields.\n- Constraint block carries the exact spec-derived semantics (\"never the secret value\", \"Do not document a value-in-env behavior\") — no authoring ambiguity for the executor.\n\n## Summary\n\nStrong, well-scoped documentation-only prompt with accurate cross-prompt contract references, a self-contained verification set, and correct container/operator boundary handling. Two minor recommendations (summary has 4 bullets rather than the DoD's 5; `readme-guide.md` would be a more targeted doc reference) and one informational ordering note. No critical issues; safe to approve after the minor tweaks."}],"resolvedModel":"deepseek-v4-flash[1m]","totalDurationMs":138847,"totalTokens":57632,"totalToolUseCount":24,"usage":{"input_tokens":60,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1280,"cache_read_input_tokens":51200,"output_tokens":5092,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"toolStats":{"readCount":6,"searchCount":0,"bashCount":18,"editFileCount":0,"linesAdded":0,"linesRemoved":0,"otherToolCount":0}}}
